00:37:25,200 --> 00:37:40,080
[SPEAKER_00] And so if you can build a feature into the app, and you gotta be careful because this can be a trap as well as like a really fun TikTok video doesn't necessarily mean that it's a great product feature that delivers value and stays core to the app and everything like that.

335
00:37:40,880 --> 00:37:42,160
[SPEAKER_00] But it is a fun filter to think through.

336
00:37:42,320 --> 00:37:54,160
[SPEAKER_00] I talked to the 11 Labs team on the podcast a few weeks ago and they were talking about how they write the tweet before they build the product and thinking through, like, what are people going to care about?

337
00:37:54,320 --> 00:37:55,040
[SPEAKER_00] What's the hook?

338
00:37:55,200 --> 00:37:57,920
[SPEAKER_00] What's the three second demonstration?

339
00:37:58,240 --> 00:38:08,160
[SPEAKER_00] And so many of the apps that we do see going viral and doing really well with UGC, it's because they have those hooks and it can just be such a powerful thing.

340
00:38:09,200 --> 00:38:11,360
[SPEAKER_01] Yeah, it's almost like the new version of the Amazon memo.

341
00:38:11,520 --> 00:38:22,000
