342
00:38:22,240 --> 00:38:24,000
[SPEAKER_01] But people's attention spans have gotten so much shorter.

343
00:38:24,400 --> 00:38:28,880
[SPEAKER_01] So now instead of a news article, it's a tweet.

344
00:38:29,520 --> 00:38:30,880
[SPEAKER_00] Or a TikTok video, yeah.

345
00:38:31,200 --> 00:38:39,040
[SPEAKER_01] And it is really helpful to start with the end in mind because the reality is no matter how good your product is, if people aren't willing to give it a chance, it won't matter.

346
00:38:39,280 --> 00:38:41,600
[SPEAKER_01] It's like a tree falls in the forest and nobody is there to hear it.

347
00:38:41,760 --> 00:38:42,320
[SPEAKER_01] Did it really happen?

348
00:38:42,480 --> 00:38:48,160
[SPEAKER_01] And so you need to start with the end in mind, which is how are you going to get your first hundred or first thousand users?

349
00:38:48,480 --> 00:38:54,560
[SPEAKER_01] And part of that is, you know, writing the tweet in advance or figuring out what the TikTok video needs to look like in advance.

350
00:38:54,960 --> 00:39:09,840
[SPEAKER_00] And to bring it back to AI and the theme of this podcast is that these new experiences that are enabled by AI, like we talked about with CalAI, like that was their hook, was like, you know, they show a picture of like, yeah, I'm tracking my macros, but look how easy it is.

351
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:14,720
